#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.5 Overview]

#h(36pt)This activity was conducted as part of the Swachh Bharat Initiative of the Government of India with the objective of promoting cleanliness, environmental responsibility, and awareness among students and the public. The activity was held at Tannirbhavi Beach, Mangaluru, in association with the Department of Tourism, Mangalore, where students actively participated in maintaining cleanliness and contributing towards a cleaner environment.

#h(36pt)The programme focused on creating awareness about the importance of keeping public places and coastal areas clean. During the activity, participants took part in beach cleaning and removal of waste, helping to reduce litter and maintain the cleanliness of the surrounding area.

#h(36pt)The activity also provided an opportunity to understand the harmful effects of improper waste disposal on the environment, particularly on marine and coastal ecosystems. Students were encouraged to adopt responsible waste-management practices and to motivate others to maintain cleanliness in their surroundings.

#h(36pt)Active participation in the Swachh Bharat activity helped develop a sense of social responsibility, environmental awareness, teamwork, and civic responsibility among the participants. The programme emphasized that maintaining cleanliness is a collective responsibility and that small individual efforts can contribute significantly to environmental protection.

#h(36pt)Overall, the activity successfully promoted the objectives of the Swachh Bharat Mission by encouraging cleanliness, responsible waste disposal, and awareness about protecting public and natural spaces.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.6 Use of Technology]

- Use of mobile phones/cameras to document the cleanliness activity.
- Digital platforms can be used to create awareness about cleanliness and environmental protection.
- Online resources were used to understand the importance of the Swachh Bharat Initiative and proper waste management.
- Digital media can be used to spread awareness about maintaining clean beaches and public places.
- Photographs and digital documentation can be used to encourage others to participate in similar environmental activities.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.7 Sustainable Development Best Practices]

- Promoting clean and healthy surroundings through active participation in beach cleaning.
- Supporting SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities by encouraging cleaner and more sustainable public spaces.
- Supporting SDG 14 – Life Below Water by reducing waste and pollution in coastal areas.
- Creating awareness about the harmful effects of plastic and other waste on marine ecosystems.
- Encouraging responsible waste disposal and environmentally friendly habits.
- Developing a sense of civic and environmental responsibility among students.
- Encouraging community participation in cleanliness and environmental conservation activities.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.8 Outcome of the Activity]

#h(36pt)The activity successfully contributed to maintaining the cleanliness of Tannirbhavi Beach, Mangaluru, while creating awareness about environmental protection and responsible waste management. Participation in the programme improved students' teamwork, civic responsibility, environmental awareness, and commitment towards maintaining clean public spaces. The activity also encouraged participants to adopt sustainable practices and contribute to a cleaner and healthier environment.

